  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somali constituents have increased capacity to facilitate just transitions towards environmentally sustainable economies and societies for all</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aligning with Somalia&#x2019;s National Determined Contributions (NDCs 2021-2030) and development frameworks, the intervention under CPO SOM106 seeks to mitigate climate-induced adversities, enhance community resilience, advance social justice and contribute to a just transition. 
The intervention approach aligns well with the UN Joint Programme for Sustainable Charcoal Reduction and Alternative Livelihoods (PROSCAL) Phase II, which is funded by the UN Somalia Joint Fund through UNDP and the Ministry of Environment and Climate Change. By closely collaborating with PROSCAL, the Just Transition intervention can leverage existing frameworks and resources to enhance its effectiveness. The outcomes of PROSCAL Phase II&#x2014;focused on revitalizing the Somali economy, enhancing livelihoods, and generating employment through inclusive growth&#x2014;provide a strong foundation upon which the Just Transition intervention can build to ensure a sustainable reduction in charcoal dependence. This integrated approach ensures that the transition not only supports environmental goals but also contributes to broader economic development and improves the health of the population, especially women, thereby making the shift away from charcoal both sustainable and beneficial for all stakeholders involved. 
In addition, the intervention is part of the implementation of the new federal law on environmental protection and management which was ratified by Parliament and signed into law by the President in February 2024. This Law states, in the article 55 dedicated to just transition, that Somalia acknowledges the need for a Just Transition especially for those directly affected by climate change and tasked the Federal Minister of Environment and Climate change with developing and implementing a Just Transition Policy. The Law clearly mentions that &#x201c;the Principles of Just Transition shall be realised through inclusive social dialogue among all sectors of the society affected by climate change including the pr</narrative>
  </description>
